// `--fix` writes only to the program's own files. A file its build program generates is
// written again by every build, so a fix in it is said and not made, and its error stays;
// the same error in the program's own file is fixed.
//# $ ctxc check --fix {dir}
//# exit: 1
//# stderr:
//| {dir}/src/main.ctx:2:5: fixed: discard the result
//| -     made::n{}
//| +     _ = made::n{}
//| {work:.}/gen/g/made.ctx:4:9: not fixed: discard the result: the file is std's or one the build program generates, not the program's own
//| {work:.}/gen/g/made.ctx:4:10: error: the result of `n` (i64) is unused: use it, or discard it with `_ = ...`
//| check: 1 error; not checked until the program has no other error: the order of a call's fields, what tasks borrow, consts computed by running code
//# file src/main.ctx:
//| fn main { mut io: Io } {
//|     _ = made::n{}
//|     io::println_i64{ &io, n = made::twice{} }
//| }
